3,1,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Midori,,"We need to agree on what ""success"" actually looks like before we pick a vendor.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,Success means the yard keeps moving when the office is in chaos.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I’d rather not pick a vendor that just ages quietly in place like our last one did.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I’m worried about the people who actually run the depots.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m less interested in the sticker price and more in the bill that arrives after the contract is signed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that post-contract bill is exactly the kind of drift I’m worried about.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, quiet aging is a symptom. The root cause is usually a system that can’t survive our actual yard conditions.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, fair point, but a system that can’t survive the yard is just a more expensive way to age.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, the yard is only half the story. If the people running it are already stretched thin, no system survives the rollout.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, agreed. But if the system is too complex, we’ll just hire more people to manage the mess, which costs more.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, complexity is a cost, but so is a system that breaks the moment the business changes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, true, but a system that breaks on change is one we can’t afford to fix mid-peak.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, exactly. We can’t afford downtime, but we also can’t afford a system that needs constant patching.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, constant patching is a symptom of poor design, not a solution. We need stability, not just activity.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, stability is nice, but if the design is rigid, we pay for it in endless workarounds.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. Rigid systems create hidden costs. Let’s look into the upgrade history and the support ownership to see where we’ve been hurt before.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I’ll check the depot calendar and the yard devices. We need to know if the hardware can even handle the new software.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,May,,"@Midori, I’ll pull the 2018 pay move data and the warehouse rule changes. I want to see how badly external help and shifting rules have burned us before.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, I’ll look into the administrator retirements and the depot supervisors. I need to know who is left to carry this, and how the last rollout actually landed on the floor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, I’ll review the board minutes and the renewal invoices. I need to see how we’ve been tricked by the pricing structure before.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
25,1,,action,Midori,,Upgrade history of the dispatch tool; Support ownership during last winter's outage,"{""action"":""investigate"",""cards"":[""card_05"",""card_03""],""parse"":""ok""}"
